														<r3d:remarks>The database is extensively cross-referenced. The ChEBI index is used to resolve any synonyms or cross references. Reactions are currently linked to the EC list, KEGG and MetaCyc, and the reactions will be used in the IntEnz database and in all relevant UniProtKB entries. Furthermore, the reactions will also be used in the UniPathway database to generate pathways and metabolic networks.</r3d:remarks>
